tic plugin marketplace for AI coding tools with 94 plugins, 203 domain expert agents, 175 modular skills, and 109 commands. Supports Claude Code, Codex CLI, Cursor, OpenCode, GitHub Copilot, and Gemini CLI from a single Markdown source.\n   254→                    </div>\n   255→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   256→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   257→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   258→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-24</span>\n   259→                    </div>\n   260→                </div>\n   261→\n   262→                <div class=\"item\">\n   263→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   264→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/UfoMiao/zcf\">ZCF (Zero-Config Code Flow)</a>\n   265→                    </div>\n   266→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   267→                        Zero-config, one-click setup for Claude Code & Codex with bilingual support, intelligent agent system and personalized AI assistant. Supports 10+ popular AI coding tools with TypeScript-based workflow automation.\n   268→                    </div>\n   269→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   270→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   271→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   272→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-30</span>\n   273→                    </div>\n   274→                </div>\n   275→\n   276→                <div class=\"item\">\n   277→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   278→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Nano-Collective/nanocoder\">Nanocoder</a>\n   279→                    </div>\n   280→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   281→                        An open-source terminal-based AI coding assistant built by a community collective. Features multi-provider support (Ollama, OpenRouter, Anthropic, Google), local-first architecture with privacy focus, and no paid tiers or closed-source features.\n   282→                    </div>\n   283→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   284→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   285→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   286→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-30</span>\n   287→                    </div>\n   288→                </div>\n   289→\n   290→                <div class=\"item\">\n   291→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   292→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/automagik-dev/genie\">Genie</a>\n   293→                    </div>\n   294→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   295→                        CLI agent that interviews users, plans work, dispatches parallel agents in isolated worktrees, and reviews code before presenting results. 'Wishes in, PRs out' with integration support for Claude Code, Codex, Warp, and Hermes.\n   296→                    </div>\n   297→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   298→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   299→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   300→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-08-01</span>\n   301→                    </div>\n   302→                </div>\n   303→\n   304→                <div class=\"item\">\n   305→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   306→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/phuetz/code-buddy\">Code Buddy</a>\n   307→                    </div>\n   308→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   309→                        Open-source multi-provider AI coding agent with terminal + Electron desktop interfaces. Features local-first execution on Ollama, 15 LLM providers with automatic failover, ~110 tools, and 24/7 multi-AI fleet capabilities.\n   310→                    </div>\n   311→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   312→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   313→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   314→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-25</span>\n   315→                    </div>\n   316→                </div>\n   317→\n   318→                <div class=\"item\">\n   319→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   320→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/VAMFI/claude-user-memory\">Claude User Memory</a>\n   321→                    </div>\n   322→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   323→                        Autonomous agent substrate for Claude Code CLI implementing Research→Plan→Implement workflows with quality gates, TDD enforcement, and multi-agent coordination. Built on Anthropic's engineering research with 4.8-5.5x faster development claims.\n   324→                    </div>\n   325→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   326→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   327→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   328→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-25</span>\n   329→                    </div>\n   330→                </div>\n   331→\n   332→                <div class=\"item\">\n   333→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   334→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/feiskyer/koder\">Koder</a>\n   335→                    </div>\n   336→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   337→                        An experimental, open-source AI coding assistant for the terminal that combines a streaming TUI, persistent local sessions, durable goals and scheduled loops, repository-aware tools, extensible skills, MCP integrations, and sandbox-aware permissions in one Python runtime.\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   340→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   341→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   342→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-28</span>\n   343→                    </div>\n   344→                </div>\n   345→\n   346→                <div class=\"item\">\n   347→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   348→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/iris-networks/terminator\">Terminator</a>\n   349→                    </div>\n   350→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   351→                        A completely free opensource alternative to manus, openhands and cua. Multi-agent AI platform for code execution, research, and browser automation with standalone binary deployment.\n   352→                    </div>\n   353→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   354→                        <span class=\"category\">code agent</span>\n   355→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   356→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-27</span>\n   357→                    </div>\n   358→                </div>\n   359→\n   360→                <div class=\"item\">\n   361→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   362→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/straylabs-ai/deadend-cli\">Deadend CLI</a>\n   363→                    </div>\n   364→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   365→                        Agentic pentest tooling achieving 81% on XBOW's benchmark in full black-box. Completely self-hosted with support for every model available on LiteLLM (Ollama, Anthropic, OpenAI, etc.). Autonomous web application penetration testing agent using feedback-driven iteration.\n   366→                    </div>\n   367→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   368→                        <span class=\"category\">code agent</span>\n   369→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   370→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-22</span>\n   371→                    </div>\n   372→                </div>\n   373→\n   374→                <div class=\"item\">\n   375→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   376→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/aannoo/hcom\">Hcom</a>\n   377→                    </div>\n   378→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   379→                        CLI tool that enables AI coding agents to communicate, watch, and spawn each other across terminals. Single Rust binary with no background services. Supports Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Codex CLI, Antigravity CLI, Cursor CLI, OpenCode, Kilo, Pi, Kimi, and Copilot CLI.\n   380→                    </div>\n   381→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   382→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   383→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   384→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-21</span>\n   385→                    </div>\n   386→                </div>\n   387→\n   388→                <div class=\"item\">\n   389→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   390→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/farion1231/cc-switch\">CC-Switch</a>\n   391→                    </div>\n   392→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   393→                        A cross-platform desktop All-in-One assistant for Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, OpenClaw, Grok Build & Hermes Agent. Written in Rust using Tauri framework to provide unified interface for multiple AI coding CLI tools.\n   394→                    </div>\n   395→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   396→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   397→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   398→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-08-04</span>\n   399→                    </div>\n   400→                </div>\n   401→\n   402→                <div class=\"item\">\n   403→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   404→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/arkatom/ai-instructions\">AI Instructions</a>\n   405→                    </div>\n   406→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   407→                        CLI tool to scaffold AI development instructions for ClaudeCode, Cursor, GitHub Copilot and more. Provides complete instruction templates and 90 specialized agents for different development tasks.\n   408→                    </div>\n   409→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   410→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   411→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   412→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-08-03</span>\n   413→                    </div>\n   414→                </div>\n   415→\n   416→                <div class=\"item\">\n   417→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   418→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/aigo666/gemini-cli-new\">Gemini CLI New</a>\n   419→                    </div>\n   420→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   421→                        An open-source AI agent bringing Gemini's power directly to your terminal with native proxy API support. Features include querying and editing large codebases within Gemini's 1M token context window, multimodal capabilities, and MCP server integrations.\n   422→                    </div>\n   423→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   424→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   425→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   426→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-31</span>\n   427→                    </div>\n   428→                </div>\n   429→\n   430→                <div class=\"item\">\n   431→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   432→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/kubiks-inc/kubiks-cli\">Kubiks CLI</a>\n   433→                    </div>\n   434→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   435→                        Automatically instruments applications to capture comprehensive runtime data (logs, traces, requests, AI SDK calls) and integrates with AI code editors like Cursor through MCP to provide complete debugging context.\n   436→                    </div>\n   437→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   438→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   439→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   440→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-31</span>\n   441→                    </div>\n   442→                </div>\n   443→\n   444→                <div class=\"item\">\n   445→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   446→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/kinhunt/mcpdog\">MCPDog</a>\n   447→                    </div>\n   448→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   449→                        Universal MCP Server Manager that allows users to configure multiple MCP servers through a single interface. Features web dashboard, auto-detection, and unified proxy layer. Perfect for Claude Desktop, Claude Code, Cursor, Gemini CLI & AI assistants.\n   450→                    </div>\n   451→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   452→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   453→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   454→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-29</span>\n   455→                    </div>\n   456→                </div>\n   457→\n   458→                <div class=\"item\">\n   459→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   460→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/bobmatnyc/claude-mpm\">Claude MPM (Multi-Agent Project Manager)</a>\n   461→                    </div>\n   462→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   463→                        Workflow and agent management framework for Claude Code CLI with 47+ specialized agents, 56+ bundled skills, full MCP integration, session management, and GitHub-first SDK mode.\n   464→                    </div>\n   465→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   466→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   467→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   468→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-25</span>\n   469→                    </div>\n   470→                </div>\n   471→\n   472→                <div class=\"item\">\n   473→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   474→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/Fr-e-d/AI-Governor-Framework\">AI-Governor-Framework</a>\n   475→                    </div>\n   476→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   477→                        A governance framework designed to teach AI assistants your project's unique DNA through a rules-based system and development workflow protocols. Turn any AI coding assistant into a disciplined, project-aware engineering partner that respects your architecture and coding standards.\n   478→                    </div>\n   479→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   480→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   481→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   482→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-25</span>\n   483→                    </div>\n   484→                </div>\n   485→\n   486→                <div class=\"item\">\n   487→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   488→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/MahmoudAshours/Commentator\">Commentator</a>\n   489→                    </div>\n   490→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   491→                        Local AI-powered CLI that writes Git commit messages using staged diffs. Works entirely offline using Code Llama via Ollama with no internet, telemetry, or GitHub Copilot required.\n   492→                    </div>\n   493→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   494→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   495→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   496→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-24</span>\n   497→                    </div>\n   498→                </div>\n   499→\n   500→                <div class=\"item\">\n   501→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   502→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/PaulGG-Code/agno-cli\">Agno CLI</a>\n   503→                    </div>\n   504→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   505→                        Multi-modal AI agents living in your terminal with full modularity and customization. Features coordinated AI collaboration with role-based architecture (Leader, Worker, Contributor, Specialist, Coordinator, Observer) and comprehensive tool integration.\n   506→                    </div>\n   507→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   508→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   509→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   510→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-22</span>\n   511→                    </div>\n   512→                </div>\n   513→\n   514→                <div class=\"item\">\n   515→                    <div class=\"item-title\">\n   516→                        <a href=\"https://github.com/andrewchambers/minicoder\">Minicoder</a>\n   517→                    </div>\n   518→                    <div class=\"item-description\">\n   519→                        A minimalist AI terminal agent and assistant for Unix systems. Written in C with a tiny garbage collector, performs actions by generating shell scripts, tracks plans and todos across iterations, and manages file focus.\n   520→                    </div>\n   521→                    <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   522→                        <span class=\"category\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   523→                        <span class=\"source\">GitHub</span>\n   524→                        <span class=\"release-date\">Released: 2025-07-21</span>\n   525→                    </div>\n   526→                </div>\n   527→            </section>\n   528→\n   529→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section (35%) -->\n   530→            <section class=\"whitelist-updates column\">\n   531→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Whitelist Updates</h2>\n   532→                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   533→                    No whitelist updates available for this period.\n   534→                </div>\n   535→            </section>\n   536→\n   537→            <!-- Technical Insights Section (25%) -->\n   538→            <section class=\"technical-insights column\">\n   539→                <h2 class=\"section-header\">Technical Insights</h2>\n   540→                <div class=\"empty-section\">\n   541→                    No technical insights available for this period.\n   542→                </div>\n   543→            </section>\n   544→        </main>\n   545→\n   546→        <footer>\n   547→            <div class=\"footer-content\">\n   548→                <div>\n   549→                    Agentic Coding Research Report | Generated: 2026-08-04\n   550→                </div>\n   551→                <div class=\"footer-links\">\n   552→                    <a href=\"#\">Archive</a>\n   553→                    <a href=\"#\">About</a>\n   554→                    <a href=\"#\">Contact</a>\n   555→                </div>\n   556→            </div>\n   557→        </footer>\n   558→    </div>\n   559→</body>\n   560→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
